==History==
2023
*The Raging Prince [[Cards|card]] was made available in the [[Tournament|Raging Prince Event]] on 25/9/2023.
*On 3/10/2023, the Raging Prince was removed from the game.

== Trivia==
*The word "''Prince''" comes from the Latin word "''prīnceps''", meaning first head.
**The Raging Prince is 1 of 20 [[cards]] associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Royal Giant]], [[Royal Delivery]], [[Tower Princess]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Prince]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Princess]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Spirit Empress]], [[Super Knight]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Royal Chef]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
*The Raging Prince is shown to make the practice of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jousting jousting]. Jousting is a medieval and renaissance martial game or hastilude between two combatants either on horse or on foot. The joust became an iconic characteristic of the knight in Romantic medievalism. The participants of a joust on horseback experience close to three and a quarter times their body weight in G-forces when the lances collide with their armour. Originally, it started as the military use of lances by heavy cavalry, but was transformed into a specialized sport during the Late Middle Ages.
**He is 1 of 5 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that have a charge, the others being [[Battle Ram]], Dark Prince, Prince, and [[Ram Rider]].
***The Battle Ram's charge shares the same sound effects as the Raging Prince's, only at a lower pitch.
*The Raging Prince's pony resembles a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shetland_pony Shetland pony], a breed of ponies that has a compact body with short legs and a long mane, and is commonly ridden in horse shows.
*The Raging Prince is 1 of 8 troops that can jump over the river, the others being [[Hog Rider]], Royal Hogs, Dark Prince, Prince, Ram Rider, [[Mother Witch|Cursed Hog]], and [[Santa Hog Rider]].
*The grill covering the [[Mega Minion]]'s mouth is very similar to the visor on the Raging Prince's helmet.
*The [[Ranked|Champion League]] badge resembles the Raging Prince's helmet.
*In [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters], the [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Pi%C3%B1ata Piñata] resembles a piñata version of the Raging Prince's pony.
*The description incorrectly mentions that the Raging Prince does double damage with his charge, as at some Levels, he deals 1 more than double.

